    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d664">

                <pb facs="0688" n="584" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg584"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.111/129.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1266.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-08-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 12, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s No. 387 of
                    July 31, 1913, regarding the entrance into Haiti of persons of Syrian origin, I
                    have the honor to advise the Department that I took up the matter with the
                    President of Haiti and permitted him to read the instructions of the Department
                    on the subject.</p>
                <p>The President, after reading the Department’s instructions, stated that he was in
                    full accord therewith. I have deemed it advisable, however, to have the
                    President confirm our conversation in writing and I shall endeavor to secure
                    this confirmation within the next few days.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">H. W. Furniss</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
